From 5d12f0619cfb5786b11ef8e2a10b497f07a74e76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Nintu (agent)" <nintu@simple-host.local>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:04:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Setup assistant: redaction catches JSON keys, log prefixes,
 colour codes, quoted values, curl/mysql/--password credentials, secret
 headers, more secret names, SAS sig, UpCloud tokens and non-ASCII emails; the
 hint says to check before sending

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 CHANGELOG.md                                  |  1 +
 FEATURES.md                                   |  7 +-
 internal/handler/setupredact.go               | 61 ++++++++++-----
 internal/handler/static/privacy.html          |  2 +-
 internal/handler/static/setup/assist.js       | 29 +++++---
 .../handler/testdata/setup-redact-cases.json  | 74 ++++++++++++++++++-
 6 files changed, 142 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index f3974bba..15fffd28 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ One line per shipped change, newest first. Add a line here in the same commit as
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Setup assistant review fixes: pasted output loses more secret shapes before it is sent (JSON keys, `docker compose logs` prefixes, terminal colour codes, quoted values, `curl -uuser:pass`/`-fsSu`, `--password`, `mysql -p`, Authorization/Cookie/Set-Cookie/X-…-Key headers, `SMTP_PASS`/`*_PASSPHRASE`/`SECRET_KEY_BASE`, URL passwords with `/`, Azure SAS `sig=`, UpCloud `ucat_` tokens, non-ASCII emails), the same in the page and on the server; the hint now says we remove the ones we recognise and to check before sending.
 - **UpCloud, recommended for a small box** on https://simple-host.app/setup?product=small-box: "Where it runs" offers UpCloud (recommended) or a server you already have. UpCloud shows why (the smallest server, 1 CPU and 1 GB for about $5/month, runs Simple Host comfortably; we test on it), a **Create your UpCloud account — $25 in credits** button (a referral link, and the page says so: the credit is UpCloud's offer for new accounts through it, on their terms) and the steps: create the account, create an API user in the UpCloud control panel, answer the questions, then give your AI agent the prompt. The files step gives a one-line command that sets the API user in your own terminal (the password is not shown) and a prompt that has your agent create the smallest Ubuntu 24.04 server with `upctl` or the UpCloud API, add your SSH key, have you add the DNS records, install, check health and HTTPS and tell you the admin page; the page never asks for UpCloud credentials. The install command now fetches the installer from its pinned release instead of `main`. The advanced docs and the run-hackathon skill's install and provider pages carry the recommendation. Skills 0.26.2.
 - **Setup assistant** on https://simple-host.app/setup: an Assistant button opens a panel (beside the form on wide screens) that answers questions about the settings of the product you are setting up, fills in the form from a plain request ("Set this up for a 200-person company with Microsoft sign-in and stricter security"), and cleans up your choices ("Clean up my choices": odd values explained, conflicts flagged, resets to the default offered). Suggested changes show as "Set X to Y — why" with Apply, Ignore and Apply all; nothing changes until you apply it, applying goes through the form's own checks, and the files follow. It can also help with an error: paste the output (or open `/setup?product=…#help`), review exactly what will be sent with keys, tokens, passwords and email addresses removed, then Send for help; the answer gives the likely cause, a command to confirm it and the fix. `POST /v1/setup/assist` (same-origin, streamed like Ask) sends the model only the product, where you are in the form, the non-secret choices, the answers picked from lists, your message, the last few turns and any output you chose to send (redacted again on the server); every proposed change is checked against the settings list and never loosens a security-sensitive setting past both its default and your value. New settings `SETUP_ASSIST_DAILY_MAX` (300; 0 turns it off and hides the panel), `SETUP_ASSIST_MAX_IN_FLIGHT` (1), `SETUP_ASSIST_PER_NETWORK_DAILY` (40). Needs migration `v073-setup-assist-daily.sql`. Privacy page updated.
 - **Set it up with your AI agent**: the setup helper's files step gives one block to copy into the AI agent you use in a terminal, with what the machine needs, every step with your files in it (secrets stay blanks for the agent to ask for), how to check the result, and where to paste an error for help.
